  "body": "Part of issue 1649. The maintainer chose to split that issue in two parts (question dialog, 2026-11-14: \"Split in two\").\n\nThe maintainer's request in issue 1649: on the WCS page, under Quarter turns, add a \"Flip X\", a \"Flip Y\" and a \"Flip Z\" button. A flip reverses one axis direction (X+ becomes X-) and does not turn the gizmo about a different axis. Some machines have reversed axis directions.\n\nThis part adds the stored flip and the controls. It does not change posted G-code.\n\nScope:\n- Store one flip flag for each axis with the WCS of a setup. The WCS rotation is a unit quaternion and cannot hold a mirror, so the flags are new schema fields and new project-file keys. A project file without the keys opens with no flip.\n- Add an undoable command that sets the flags. Undo restores the previous flags.\n- Add the three buttons on the WCS page, under Quarter turns. The gizmo shows the flipped direction.\n- Add the MCP tool for the command. `get_job` shows the flags.\n- The post and toolpath generation refuse a setup with a flipped WCS by name, in the same way as they refuse a rotated WCS now (`crates/app/src/posting_wcs_rotation.rs`). The message says which axis is flipped and that posting a flipped WCS is not available yet.\n\nDone means: the three buttons set and clear the flags with undo and redo, the project file keeps the flags, the MCP tool sets them, and a post of a setup with a flip is refused by name. A test pins each point. No NC golden changes.\n",
